%I A402427 #17 Nov 22 2026 10:00:09
%S A402427 2,3,7,11,17,19,23,37,41,47,97,109,1069,1439,1721,1993,2851,3019,
%T A402427 13597,37139,37223,45533,56951
%N A402427 Primes p such that 4*p# - 1 is prime, where prime(n)# = A002110(n).
%C A402427 Primes prime(n) such that A402499(n) is prime.
%C A402427 a(24) > 10^5. - _Michael S. Branicky_, Nov 21 2026
%e A402427 8-1 = 7 is prime, so 2 is a term;
%e A402427 8*3-1 = 23 is prime, so 3 is a term;
%e A402427 8*3*5-1 = 119 = 7*17, so 5 is not a term;
%e A402427 8*3*5*7-1 = 839 is prime, so 7 is a term;
%e A402427 8*3*5*7*11-1 = 9239 is prime, so 11 is a term;
%e A402427 8*3*5*7*11*13-1 = 120119 = 113*1063, so 13 is not a term;
%e A402427 8*3*5*7*11*13*17-1 = 2042039 is prime, so 17 is a term;
%e A402427 8*3*5*7*11*13*17*19-1 = 38798759 is prime, so 19 is a term.
%o A402427 (PARI) my(P=4); forprime(p=2, 1000, P*=p; if(ispseudoprime(P-1), print1(p, ", ")))
%Y A402427 Cf. A002110 (primorials), A102476 (4 times primorials), A228698, A228699.
%Y A402427 See A402499 for a list of related sequences.
%K A402427 nonn,more,new
%O A402427 1,1
%A A402427 _Jianing Song_, Nov 18 2026
